"[{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/postal_address/\",\"len\":735,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesPostal Address ModuleOn this pagePostal Address Module Introduction​ Ask for a postal address and store it in your CRM. Typical Use Cases​ Attributes such as postal address are required for certain application forms, where you have to enter your address. Just insert the module postal address to your agent and save the input as a variable. How to Use the Module​ Intro​ Add an intro to introduce before asking for a postal address. Other texts​ Choose placeholder for the form. Sign in​ The consumer must be signed in. Useful Tips​ The zipcode by default is allowed to have an arbitrary pattern. If you only want to allow 5-digit numbers, under input validation you can enter following regular expression pattern: [0-9]{5}\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"s are required for certain application forms, where you have to enter your address. Just insert the module postal address to your agent and save the input as a variable. How to Use the Module​ Intro​ Add an intro to introduce before asking for a postal address. Other texts​ Choose placeholder for the form. Sign in​ The\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/prizes/\",\"len\":1059,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesPrizes Gallery ModuleOn this pagePrizes Gallery Module Introduction​ Display multiple prizes for raffles or sweepstakes. Typical Use Cases​ Enhance your raffle by allowing participants to view prizes before engaging, or they can skip directly to the questionnaire. How to Use the Module​ Add Prize​ Add as many prizes as you'd like, providing each with a name, description, and image. Prize Visibility​ Each prize can be shown within a defined start and end time window. Adjusting Text Case for Form Titles​ You can adjust the text transformation for the Prizes Gallery in the Branding section, under Form title and then Title. Choose 'Uppercase' for all capital letters or 'None' for normal capitalization. Other Texts​ Customize all relevant text fields according to your needs. tipThe Prizes Module is designed to display prizes but does not handle actual prize redemption. For prize redemption, consider using other modules like the Loyalty Redemption module, which enables customers to claim rewards based on their accumulated loyalty points.\",\"imgs\":[\"prizes_gallery_time-204f6aa696ad1ff9e1815dbf4d641ab0.png|prizes_gallery_time\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/pro_campaign/\",\"len\":244,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProCampaign ModuleOn this pageProCampaign Module Integrate ProCampaign into your process. ProCampaign Cookie​ You can listen for ProCampaign cookies on your Website by adding an API key in the top right corner of the process module.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/proceed/\",\"len\":1431,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProceed Question ModuleOn this pageProceed Question Module Introduction​ The Proceed Question Module prompts customers to decide if they want to continue with the chat. This process module helps structure the chat flow into well-organized segments, ensuring that users remain engaged without being overwhelmed. Typical Use Cases​ This module is particularly useful in the following scenarios: After a series of informational messages where the customer has not actively participated, use this module as a Call-to-Action (CTA) to re-engage the user. When you want to break the chat flow into manageable sections, allowing customers to process information before moving forward. How to Use the Module​ Placement: Insert the module after a sequence of messages to give users a moment to decide if they want to continue. Customization: Choose between the provided template text or enter your own text to prompt the user. Example Usage​ Consider a scenario where your agent provides a series of tips or instructions. To ensure the user is ready to proceed and not overloaded with information, you can use the Proceed Question module to ask if they would like to continue. Question: \\\"Would you like to continue to the next tip?\\\" Proceed button text: \\\"Yes, continue\\\" (proceeds to the next step) By incorporating the Proceed Question module in this way, you maintain user engagement and manage the information flow effectively.\",\"imgs\":[\"|proceed_demo\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"hoose between the provided template text or enter your own text to prompt the user. Example Usage​ Consider a scenario where your agent provides a series of tips or instructions. To ensure the user is ready to proceed and not overloaded with information, you can use the Proceed Question module to ask if they would like\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/process_instance_create/\",\"len\":301,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesCreate Process Instance ModuleOn this pageCreate Process Instance Module Introduction​ Use this if customers should be able to go through the same agent several times. For tech experts, this creates a new namespace. Only works with process-specific variables, not with process-independent.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"stance ModuleOn this pageCreate Process Instance Module Introduction​ Use this if customers should be able to go through the same agent several times. For tech experts, this creates a new namespace. Only works with process-specific variables, not with process-independent.\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/product_feed/\",\"len\":3535,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleOn this pageProduct Feed Module Introduction​ Present the products of your external data feed to customers. An external data source can be connected to LoyJoy using a connector. Typical Use Cases​ The Product Feed module is a powerful tool for displaying a list of up to 12 products that best match your customer's preferences, as determined by a preceding chat flow. The module's key advantage lies in its integration of a recommender, which automatically pulls content from various connectors. This continuous update ensures that your customers receive the most up-to-date and relevant product listings. How to Use the Module​ To use the module, you first have to upload your products or provide them as a Google Sheet or JSON API. Then, the products can be displayed in the chat. To control, which products are shown, there are two primary options: the tag recommender and SQL-based filters in the connectors. The tag recommender is a simple way to filter products based on tags assigned to the customer during the chat flow. For most use-cases you should use SQL-based filters as they offer more fine-grained control. Check out the guide for more information on how to set up a product database and use it for different use cases, such as location search or contact search. Connectors​ To use the Product Feed module, you need to connect your external data source. LoyJoy supports three types of connectors: Database, JSON, and Google Sheets. Learn how to use a con\",\"imgs\":[\"sheet_example-6d78145ae84ebe068925cfb00c271bdb.png|Example sheet\",\"connectors2-76a2f995f90fdd377da557d23fd9ac6d.png|Connectors\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"atch your customer's preferences, as determined by a preceding chat flow. The module's key advantage lies in its integration of a recommender, which automatically pulls content from various connectors. This continuous update ensures that your customers receive the most up-to-date and relevant product listings. How to U\",\"PI. Then, the products can be displayed in the chat. To control, which products are shown, there are two primary options: the tag recommender and SQL-based filters in the connectors. The tag recommender is a simple way to filter products based on tags assigned to the customer during the chat flow. For most use-cases yo\",\" website for product purchase. While the \\\"description,\\\" \\\"price,\\\" \\\"image_url,\\\" and \\\"url\\\" fields are not mandatory, they are highly recommended for an optimal user agent. See here for an example Google Sheet. As described, the first row is expected to hold the column names. Using Database and JSON Connectors​ For Databas\"],\"nh\":4},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/product_feed/connectors/\",\"len\":3114,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleConnectorsOn this pageConnectors LoyJoy provides the option to establish a connection with your external data source (such as Google Sheets) through connectors, allowing you to use this data within LoyJoy. LoyJoy currently offers two types of connectors. Google Sheets JSON Api Database connector For assistance with the configuration, please reach out to our support team. SQL Filter​ For connectors it is possible to define customizable filters using Structured Query Language (SQL). This allows you to filter the data from the external source before using it in LoyJoy. Take a look at the following SQL query. SELECT * FROM products WHERE title = 'Product 1'; In this example, the SQL query filters the data from the external source to only include products with the title \\\"Product 1\\\". You can use this feature to filter the data according to your requirements. Supported Operators​ Equals​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE title = 'Product 1'; Not Equals​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE title != 'Product 1'; Greater Than​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE price_euro_cent > 10099; Greater Than or Equals​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE price_euro_cent >= 10099; Less Than​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE price_euro_cent < 10099; Less Than or Equals​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE price_euro_cent <= 10099; Like​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE title LIKE 'Product%'; Not Like​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE title NOT LIKE 'Product%'; In​ SELECT * FROM products WHERE title IN ('Produc\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/product_feed/connectors/database/\",\"len\":410,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleConnectorsDatabase ConnectorDatabase Connector As an alternative to any external data source, you can use the database connector that connects to LoyJoy's database to store and retrieve products for the Product Feed Module. This connector is meant to programmatically provide information about your products. You find more information for using this API in the API documentation.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/product_feed/connectors/google_sheets/\",\"len\":738,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleConnectorsGoogle SheetsGoogle Sheets LoyJoy offers the possibility to link your Google Sheets data using a google sheet conector. To establish this connection, please follow the steps below: Authorize LoyJoy to access your Google Sheet by clicking on the \\\"Authorize\\\" button. Make sure you are logged in with the Google account that has access to the Google Sheet you want to connect to. Obtain your sheets ID and paste it in the connector settings in LoyJoy. Go to your Google Sheet and copy the ID from the URL. The ID is the long string of letters and numbers between \\\"/d/\\\" and \\\"/edit\\\" in the URL. Get your Sheet name from your Google Sheet e.g. \\\"Sheet1\\\" and paste it in your connector settings in LoyJoy.\",\"imgs\":[\"sheet_id_url-860f7d593da1415066a7fe4b238df943.png|Google Sheets URL with the Sheet ID portion between /d/ and /edit highlighted.\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/product_feed/connectors/json_api/\",\"len\":903,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleConnectorsJSON ApiJSON Api To create a JSON connector, it is recommended to use a hyperscaler such as Google Cloud or Amazon Web Services (AWS). Please consider the following code snippet of a Google Cloud Function that retrieves a feed of products to be used in the Product Feed module. For persistence, it is recommended to use a managed database, such as Google Datastore. const functions = require('@google-cloud/functions-framework')functions.http('productFeed', (req, res) => { const products = [ { title: 'Product 1', description: 'Product 1 description', price: '€10.99', url: 'https://example.com/product-1', tags: ['tag1', 'tag2'] }, { title: 'Product 2', description: 'Product 2 description', price: '€20.99', url: 'https://example.com/product-2', tags: ['tag1', 'tag3'] } ] res.setHeader('Content-type', 'application/json') res.send(JSON.stringify(products))})\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleConnectorsJSON ApiJSON Api To create a JSON connector, it is recommended to use a hyperscaler such as Google Cloud or Amazon Web Services (AWS). Please consider the following code snippet of a Google Cloud Function that retrieves a feed of products to\",\"nippet of a Google Cloud Function that retrieves a feed of products to be used in the Product Feed module. For persistence, it is recommended to use a managed database, such as Google Datastore. const functions = require('@google-cloud/functions-framework')functions.http('productFeed', (req, res) => { const products = \"],\"nh\":2},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/product_feed/tag_recommender/\",\"len\":2563,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleUsing the Tag RecommenderOn this pageUsing the Tag Recommender The tag recommender feature provides customers with the most relevant product listings, enhancing their shopping agent. infoThe tag recommender is less powerful than SQL-based filtering and should only be used for simple use cases. For more complex filtering, we recommend using SQL-based filters in the connectors. Enabling the Tag Recommender​ To activate the tag recommender, follow these steps: Navigate to the Product Feed Module. Scroll to the top of the page. You will find three options: Off, Filter, and Smart. By default, the recommender is turned off. Tag Recommender Options​ The tag recommender offers three distinct options: 1. Off​ When set to \\\"Off,\\\" all products are displayed, regardless of the assigned tags and customer preferences. This option provides an unfiltered view of your products. 2. Filter​ Selecting the \\\"Filter\\\" option displays only those products with exact matching tags. Products without matching tags are not shown, ensuring precise product recommendations. 3. Smart​ With the \\\"Smart\\\" option, products are sorted based on the number of matching tags. Products with more matching tags are displayed first, offering a personalized and tailored shopping agent. noteThe variable product_feed_result_count will be set to tell you how many products where found in the product feed with the filter applied, if applicable. Show Maximum One Product per Group​ You can choose to d\",\"imgs\":[\"Tag_2-1962d46e3fbfab0d4bb9764e5f6b5019.gif|Recommender Step 1\",\"Tag_1-0747f1e989e39a0fd113ea4d7a70f205.gif|Recommender Step 2\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"BPMN ModulesProduct Feed ModuleUsing the Tag RecommenderOn this pageUsing the Tag Recommender The tag recommender feature provides customers with the most relevant product listings, enhancing their shopping agent. infoThe tag recommend\",\" Tag Recommender The tag recommender feature provides customers with the most relevant product listings, enhancing their shopping agent. infoThe tag recommender is less powerful than SQL-based filtering and should only be used for simple use cases. For more complex filtering, we recommend using SQL-based filters in the\",\"ecommender is less powerful than SQL-based filtering and should only be used for simple use cases. For more complex filtering, we recommend using SQL-based filters in the connectors. Enabling the Tag Recommender​ To activate the tag recommender, follow these steps: Navigate to the Product Feed Module. Scroll to the top\"],\"nh\":9},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/products/\",\"len\":4301,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProduct Gallery ModuleOn this pageProduct Gallery Module Introduction​ Present your products to customers in a variety of ways. Give a product description, the price or a consumer rating together in one gallery. Animate your customers to buy your product by embedding a link behind the “Buy now” button. Typical Use Cases​ Useful to integrate into your agent to show your products or services. Multiple products will be shown in a gallery slider. Use this module to present personalized product offerings as e.g. skin care routines with your products or to show the variety of your services. How to Use the Module​ Add product​ Start by inserting the module into your editor and add one or multiple products as seen below. Product image​ Start by choosing an image orientation at the top of the products. The orientation refers to all products equally. Continue by adding a picture according to the px size you have picked above. Remember that we do not recommend your pictures be no larger than 500 KB in order to ensure a quick loading. Input fields​ Fill in the fields you think are important. Let’s start with essential input fields such as the product name, the product description, and the product link. You can see below how this information is placed. The link enables your customers to click on the product in order to get to your website. All other input fields are optional. But let us give your customers a little more information with the topline and the fold-out text. Our p\",\"imgs\":[\"intro-17d5ece193cec1d6d69fef491c3b50d1.gif|Product Example\",\"image_orientation_small-b90859553f8413d769212bb35a11131f.png|Product Image Example\",\"product_name-e152f0d9539191b3f559f44752189a47.png|Product Input Field Example\",\"product_topline-98b0a0fc45f250b362172d2db0bcd70f.png|Product Input Topline Example\",\"price-e258ef92e7fc4f55fefef550aecc3bf6.png|Product Price Example\",\"button-75616e6107fb78dfde28192194a71706.png|Product Button Example\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"r customers to buy your product by embedding a link behind the “Buy now” button. Typical Use Cases​ Useful to integrate into your agent to show your products or services. Multiple products will be shown in a gallery slider. Use this module to present personalized product offerings as e.g. skin care routines with your p\",\"ers to all products equally. Continue by adding a picture according to the px size you have picked above. Remember that we do not recommend your pictures be no larger than 500 KB in order to ensure a quick loading. Input fields​ Fill in the fields you think are important. Let’s start with essential input fields such as\",\"on for the customer to “Buy now”. The button is also able to set a variable in case you want to use the product selection in your agent's flow later on. Background​ Add a background image or choose a color that will be shown in the background.If you add an image and a color for your gradient, only the gradient will be \"],\"nh\":9},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/profiling_opt_in/\",\"len\":2893,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesProfiling Opt-In ModuleOn this pageProfiling Opt-In Module Introduction​ This module allows customers to opt-in for profiling, either through a single opt-in or a GDPR-compliant double opt-in. The double opt-in process requires email confirmation by clicking a link, ensuring full consent. Typical Use Case​ Comply with GDPR regulations by obtaining explicit consent from customers before profiling. Automate the process of sending reminder emails for customers who have not yet opted in. How to Use the Module​ Email Requirement: Ensure the customer's email address is known through an Email module or Sign-in module placed earlier in the process. Single or Double Opt-In: Configure the opt-in method—single or double. Email Template: Customize the double opt-in (DOI) email using an HTML email template. Re-ask Frequency: If the opt-in is denied, configure the module to ask again after a set number of days. Opt-In Process​ Single Opt-In: Users confirm their consent within the chat. Double Opt-In: Can be enabled or disabled. When enabled, a confirmation email is sent. If disabled, it operates as a single opt-in. These settings can be combined as needed. You can customize the DOI email body with an HTML email template. More details on email configuration can be found below. Ensure the confirmation email contains ${add_optin_url} to include the necessary link. To use this properly, embed it in a button or an <a> tag like so: <a href=\\\"${add_optin_url}\\\">Give Opt-In</a>. Under GD\",\"imgs\":[\"profiling_opt_in_demo-c30cbb13e2286da3c6df1c64bad18593.png|profiling_opt_in_demo\",\"profiling_opt_in_data-045b3ba011c23810e0ad4b9342a81b2c.png|profiling_opt_in_data\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/pub_sub/\",\"len\":2136,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesGoogle Pub/Sub ModuleOn this pageGoogle Pub/Sub Module Introduction​ Google Pub/Sub is a messaging service for exchanging event data among applications and services. It provides a reliable and scalable way to manage event-driven communication in your cloud infrastructure. With the Google Pub/Sub module in LoyJoy, you can integrate your agent with Google Pub/Sub to publish data in real-time for further processing and analysis. How to Use the Module​ Integration​ To successfully establish the connection to Google Pub/Sub, you need to provide the following fields: Project in the Google Cloud Platform: The ID of your Google Cloud project. Pub/Sub Topic: The topic in Pub/Sub to which messages will be published. Pub/Sub Service Account Credentials (JSON): The credentials file for your service account in JSON format. Steps to Set Up the Module:​ Create a Topic in Google Cloud Platform Navigate to the Pub/Sub section in the Google Cloud Console. Click \\\"Create Topic\\\" and provide a name for your topic. Set Up a Service Account Go to the \\\"IAM & Admin\\\" section and select \\\"Service Accounts.\\\" Create a new service account and assign it the \\\"Pub/Sub Editor\\\" role. Generate a JSON key for this service account and download the file. Configure the LoyJoy Module Enter your Google Cloud Platform project ID in the \\\"Project\\\" field. Provide the name of your Pub/Sub topic in the \\\"Pub/Sub Topic\\\" field. Paste the JSON content from your downloaded key file into the \\\"Service Account Credential\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\" manage event-driven communication in your cloud infrastructure. With the Google Pub/Sub module in LoyJoy, you can integrate your agent with Google Pub/Sub to publish data in real-time for further processing and analysis. How to Use the Module​ Integration​ To successfully establish the connection to Google Pub/Sub, yo\",\"d: lottery_entry Additional Information​ Source Expression: This is used to declare what information will be transmitted from the agent to google. Target Field: This is the field in the Pub/Sub message where the data will be written. Useful Tips​ Message Format: Ensure that your message format in Pub/Sub aligns with th\"],\"nh\":2},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/quiz/\",\"len\":1215,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesQuiz ModuleOn this pageQuiz Module Introduction​ Let customers play a fun quiz, add animations to make it really joyful. The following build the quiz seen below. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Add a Quiz​ Start by dragging the Quiz Module into the chat flow, then add a Quiz. You can add multiple Quizzes that can run at predefined times. Add a start and end date for when the Quiz should run. If you add multiple Quizzes without specifying start and end dates, by default, the Quizzes will follow each other in the chat flow. Add question​ Add a question to start the quiz. You can add as many questions as you want to. Make the Quiz more joyful by entering a fun intro text and adding a picture to the question! Add answer​ Add answer options that the customers can choose between. By clicking on the settings symbol you can choose if this answer should be a free text answer. Set which answer is the correct answer and add an animation and our fairydust to show the user that he has picked the right answer. Other texts​ Finally, add the texts that will be sent if the customer enters an invalid answer, if no quiz question is configured or if the chat offers to answer the question again.\",\"imgs\":[\"quiz_add-a30204d6753793697daa62fc377e41ec.gif|Add Quiz\",\"quiz_question-e28cbdcde05730456b03a68938cace08.png|Add Question\",\"quiz_answer-19f26e0775cb2fa4525af8cf883d677f.png|Add Answer\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/rapidmail/\",\"len\":1132,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesRapidmail ModuleOn this pageRapidmail Module Introduction​ The Rapidmail Module allows you to add a recipient to a recipient list in Rapidmail. infoThe email address is taken automatically from the LoyJoy variables. You need to use either an Email Module or a Sign In Module to let users enter their email address so that it can be used in the Optimizely module. How to Use the Module​ Authentication​ To authenticate, create an API key in Rapidmail instead of using your personal username and password. Use this key for secure communication. warningFor security reasons you should never enter your own username and password! Modes of Operation​ Add Recipient: Recipient List ID: Requires Recipient List ID` found in the Rapidmail URL. Double Opt-In: Select \\\"New\\\" as the Recipient Status and enable Send Activation Email to send a confirmation email via Rapidmail. Mappings​ Configure mappings to add more data fields to the recipient list. Available fields include firstname, lastname, gender, zip, and others. Use these in your email templates. For a complete list of fields, check out the Rapidmail API documentation.\",\"imgs\":[\"recpipient_list-06d5940a7b8b5a6a7a96759967675765.png|Rapidmail Recipient List ID\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/reach_five/\",\"len\":1163,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesReachFive ModuleOn this pageReachFive Module This module allows customers to authenticate in the chat with an user account from ReachFive based on OAuth 2.0. Typical Use Cases​ Use this module to authenticate users in the chat, access their ReachFive profile information, and personalize the chat agent accordingly. How to Use the Module​ Configure Redirect URIs: Add the following redirect URIs to your ReachFive settings: https://app-stable.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback https://app-runtime.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback https://runtime.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback Enter ReachFive Credentials: In the LoyJoy module, input your: ReachFive URL Client ID Client Secret Scope Customize Texts: Modify the text for the sign-in button and login prompts under \\\"Other Texts\\\" in the LoyJoy platform. Mappings​ In the mappings, configure source fields to retrieve user profile information. Default fields provided by ReachFive include: address_type, company, country, email, email_verified, delivery_note, locality, phone_number, postal_code, recipient, region, street_address, title These fields are documented in ReachFive User Profile documentation.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"se Cases​ Use this module to authenticate users in the chat, access their ReachFive profile information, and personalize the chat agent accordingly. How to Use the Module​ Configure Redirect URIs: Add the following redirect URIs to your ReachFive settings: https://app-stable.loyjoy.com/auth/oauth2/callback https://app-\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/redemptions/\",\"len\":1767,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesLoyalty Redemption ModuleOn this pageLoyalty Redemption Module Introduction​ The Loyalty Redemption Module allows customers to redeem loyalty points by storing their redemptions in a dedicated table. This enables the exchange of loyalty points for rewards. Typical Use Cases​ Manual Redemption Process: Ideal for handling redemptions that require manual intervention, such as sending physical rewards to customers. Automated Redemption Process: For an automated approach, consider using the Coupon Code process module to issue coupon codes in exchange for loyalty points. How to Use the Module​ Points Deduction​ Specify the number of points to be deducted for each redemption. You can set limits on how many times a customer can redeem points, both individually and collectively across all customers. Examples: Per Customer Limit: Allow each customer to redeem a reward only once. Overall Limit: Limit the total number of redemptions available to all customers to 100. Redemption Records​ Viewing Redemptions: The module allows you to view all redemption records, which are automatically deleted after 60 days for data privacy. CSV Export: You can export the redemption data as a CSV file for further processing, such as fulfilling physical rewards. Other Texts​ You can customize the module’s messages under \\\"Other Texts,\\\" including: Confirmation when a redemption is successful. Notifications when a customer cannot redeem again. Alerts if a customer lacks sufficient points for a rede\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/region/\",\"len\":566,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesRegion ModuleOn this pageRegion Module Introduction​ You can make regions available for selection and exclude certain regions from using the agent. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Add region​ Add as many regions as you want to. Set at every region if it is permitted to use the agent. Process-Specific Variables​ This module generates variables that are accessible throughout the current process. They are only valid for this specific process and may evolve with platform updates. For a detailed list, check the process-specific variables list.\",\"imgs\":[\"region_not_permitted_demo-6eadfd0862ec04a36364ab82971db677.png|region_not_permitted_demo\",\"region_permitted_demo-d637964679e704a870afa8b7c32a0318.png|region_permitted_demo\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"leOn this pageRegion Module Introduction​ You can make regions available for selection and exclude certain regions from using the agent. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Add region​ Add as many regions as you want to. Set at every region if it is permitted to use the agent. Process-Specific Variables​ This mod\",\"e Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Add region​ Add as many regions as you want to. Set at every region if it is permitted to use the agent. Process-Specific Variables​ This module generates variables that are accessible throughout the current process. They are only valid for this specific process and may evolve with platf\"],\"nh\":2},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/reminder_opt_in/\",\"len\":3283,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesReminder Opt-In ModuleOn this pageReminder Opt-In Module Introduction​ This module allows you to obtain customer consent to send reminders, such as appointment notifications or new advent calendar doors, in a GDPR-compliant way. You can configure single or double opt-ins, ensuring that customer consent is properly recorded.s Typical Use Case​ Gather GDPR-compliant consent from customers to send reminders for appointments or periodic notifications. Automate reminder opt-ins and manage consent seamlessly within your chat flow. How to Use the Module​ Email Requirement​ This module requires the customer’s email address. You can collect it using the Email module or Sign-in module before proceeding with the opt-in. Opt-In Process​ Single Opt-In: Automatic: The opt-in is triggered without further user interaction. Manual: Users confirm their consent within the chat. Double Opt-In: Can be enabled or disabled. When enabled, a confirmation email is sent. If disabled, it operates as a single opt-in. You can customize the DOI email body with an HTML email template. More details on email configuration can be found below. Ensure the confirmation email contains ${add_optin_url} to include the necessary link. To use this properly, embed it in a button or an <a> tag like so: <a href=\\\"${add_optin_url}\\\">Give Opt-In</a>. Under GDPR, a double opt-in (DOI) is mandatory for email marketing consent. However, if you are handling the DOI process through external systems, it can be benefici\",\"imgs\":[\"reminder_opt_in_data-59d501d3a66e0cb8d386b05f38182204.png|reminder_opt_in_data\",\"add_html-493c0dac8f3c214e0b798c65664e0253.png|add_html\",\"html_code-d36a44ed2d6a6f39223855fb5987ddbf.png|html_code\",\"confirmation-a9772c199bed46821e9d3a284952e92b.png|confirmation\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"ial for completing the DOI (Double Opt-In) process. To ensure everything is set up correctly, have a look and test it within your agent. If successful, you should receive the following response: Alternatively, you can replace the URL with one that you prefer to use. Simply paste it into the redirect section above the H\"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/reminder/\",\"len\":674,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesReminder Notification ModuleOn this pageReminder Notification Module Introduction​ Schedule a reminder notification to your customer at a certain point in time. Typical Use Cases​ For example in case of an advent calendar the chat can remind customers from 1.12. till 24.12. to open the advent calendar door. How to Use the Module​ Configure the notification settings and schedule with easy from inside the module. Useful Tips​ If the customer has given a Web push double opt-in and a reminder double opt-in before, the notification can be sent via Web push. Else if the customer has given a reminder double opt-in before, the notification can be sent via email.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/reset/\",\"len\":1476,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesSession Reset ModuleOn this pageSession Reset Module Introduction​ The Session Reset Module allows you to reset parts of the process session as needed, effectively managing the customer's session and chat histories. This module is essential for ensuring that user sessions can be cleanly restarted, preserving a seamless user agent. How to Use the Module​ Reset Options​ Reset session and variables in all agents: This action logs out the customer and drops all session variables. It's useful for starting a new session from scratch. Reset the chat history in all agents: This clears the chat history across all agents, including the current one. This is helpful for removing old conversation data. Reset the chat history in this agent: This only clears the chat history in the current agent, maintaining history in other agents. Adding Intro and Outro Texts​ You can also configure introductory and concluding texts that will be executed after the reset operation. This can enhance the user agent by providing context or additional information before and after the session reset. Intro: This text will be displayed to the user right after the session reset is performed. It can be used to explain the reason for the reset or to provide any necessary instructions. Outro: This text will be shown after the session has been reset and the Intro Text has been displayed. It can be used to confirm that the reset was successful or to guide the user on what to do next.\",\"imgs\":[\"session_reset_variables_history-725b4b60d445b44122f98820f8b6ea4a.png|session_reset_variables_history\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"and chat histories. This module is essential for ensuring that user sessions can be cleanly restarted, preserving a seamless user agent. How to Use the Module​ Reset Options​ Reset session and variables in all agents: This action logs out the customer and drops all session variables. It's useful for starting a new sess\",\" be cleanly restarted, preserving a seamless user agent. How to Use the Module​ Reset Options​ Reset session and variables in all agents: This action logs out the customer and drops all session variables. It's useful for starting a new session from scratch. Reset the chat history in all agents: This clears the chat his\",\" the customer and drops all session variables. It's useful for starting a new session from scratch. Reset the chat history in all agents: This clears the chat history across all agents, including the current one. This is helpful for removing old conversation data. Reset the chat history in this agent: This only clears \"],\"nh\":6},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/restart/\",\"len\":867,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesRestart ModuleOn this pageRestart Module Introduction​ The Restart Module allows you to restart the chatflow, so the chat begins anew from the start of the process flow. Unlike a session reset, customers will remain logged in, and the session itself is not reset. How to Use the Module​ Choose the Question Wording: Define the question that will be presented to the user to prompt the restart of the chatflow. Ensure the question is clear and concise to avoid confusion. Select the Answer Button Text: Specify the text for the answer button that the user will click to confirm the restart. This should be a clear and affirmative action text, such as \\\"Yes\\\" or \\\"Restart chat\\\". Additional Information​ Please note that all variables are retained, which can affect the chat flow. If you do not want this behavior, you should also use the session reset module.\",\"imgs\":[\"restart_question-825aafd98c26a1cfe6b55100ff8c1568.png|restart_question\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/rewards/\",\"len\":2581,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesLoyalty Rewards ModuleOn this pageLoyalty Rewards Module Introduction​ The LoyJoy Rewards Module allows you to display and manage multiple rewards within your chat agent, enabling customers to view and potentially redeem rewards based on their accumulated loyalty points. Typical Use Cases​ Display Available Rewards: Show customers the rewards they can redeem with their loyalty points. Reward Redemption Flow: Guide customers through the process of redeeming rewards, linking to relevant modules for point deduction and reward issuance. How to Use the Module​ Rewards Configuration​ You can configure multiple rewards, each displayed in a slideshow format. Each reward in the slideshow includes: Title: A short title describing the reward. Image: A visual representation of the reward. Required Loyalty Points: The number of loyalty points needed to redeem the reward. Description: An expandable section that provides more details about the reward. Redemption Button​ Each reward can have a Redemption Button, which directs the user to a selected jump target module for redeeming the reward. If no jump target is set, the button is not displayed, and the module serves as an informational display of available rewards. Important Notes​ Flow Continuation: The module does not pause for the Redemption Button to be clicked. Therefore, you should use a Stop Module or End event to hold the flow until the user interacts with the module. The button allows the flow to jump to subsequent mod\",\"imgs\":[\"rewards_display_example-2ecbccf44e16ec1eb0f0483560b8c9a1.png|rewards_display_example\",\"rewards_button_example-c8f48cd53321a4546869e97059c63fa8.png|rewards_button_example\",\"rewards_setup_example-9060e13f4e7532660842ce998584ab39.png|rewards_setup_example\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[\"Loyalty Rewards Module Introduction​ The LoyJoy Rewards Module allows you to display and manage multiple rewards within your chat agent, enabling customers to view and potentially redeem rewards based on their accumulated loyalty points. Typical Use Cases​ Display Available Rewards: Show customers the rewards they can \"],\"nh\":1},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/router_push/\",\"len\":395,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesJump to Home View ModuleOn this pageJump to Home View Module Introduction​ If a home view is configured this process module jumps to it. The jump is executed directly when the process is opened. To prevent this, place a decision jump or a continuation question before the jump. Typical Use Cases​ How to Use the Module​ Select a home view from the drop-down window inside the module.\",\"imgs\":[\"router_push-f0c66ce5b1f02b082dd27773a8a89f38.png|router push\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/salesforce_interaction_studio/\",\"len\":1018,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesSalesforce Interaction Studio ModuleOn this pageSalesforce Interaction Studio Module Introduction​ The Salesforce Interaction Studio Module allows you to send customer interaction data to Salesforce Interaction Studio, a real-time personalization and interaction management platform. This module enables the tracking and updating of customer data for enhanced personalization across channels. How to Use the Module​ Required Fields​ Dataset: Specify the dataset where the data will be sent. Salesforce Deployment: Enter only the subdomain part of your Salesforce URL (e.g., for \\\"https://abc123.salesforce.com\\\", use \\\"abc123\\\"). API Key ID: The ID for your Salesforce Interaction Studio API key. API Secret: The secret associated with your API key for authentication. For more information on how to create an API key ID and an API secret, check out the Salesforce Interaction Studio documentation Mappings​ Configure mappings to send specific customer interaction data fields to Salesforce Interaction Studio.\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/salesforce_marketing_cloud/\",\"len\":2305,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesSalesforce Marketing Cloud ModuleOn this pageSalesforce Marketing Cloud Module Introduction​ The Salesforce Marketing Cloud Module allows you to send data to Salesforce Marketing Cloud for various purposes, including ensuring a contact exists, logging interaction events, or sending messages. How to Use the Module​ warningYou will almost always need to use two Salesforce Marketing Cloud Modules in combination. First in \\\"Assure contact\\\" mode to ensure that the contact exists in Salesforce Marketing Cloud and then in either \\\"Interaction event\\\" or \\\"Send message\\\" mode to write data to Salesforce Marketing Cloud. Make sure that the customer's email address is stored in the process variable email or auth_email, otherwise \\\"Assure contact\\\" will fail. To use this module, you first have to create an integration package in Marketing Cloud. When creating the package, make sure to create a Server-to-Server integration (not \\\"Web Application\\\"). When setting up the integration also make sure the permissions are set suitable to your use-case (e.g. event permissions). In Marketing Cloud, you will also need to create e.g. a journey with an API event. This will allow you to write to a data extension and / or trigger a journey. Required Fields​ Client ID: Your Salesforce Marketing Cloud client ID. Secret: The secret associated with your client ID. Salesforce Deployment: Specify your Salesforce deployment subdomain (e.g., your-subdomain from https://your-subdomain.my.salesforce.com). Ac\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/salesforce/\",\"len\":4523,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesSalesforce Service Cloud ModuleOn this pageSalesforce Service Cloud Module Introduction​ The Salesforce Service Cloud Module integrates Salesforce Service Cloud (SFSC) into your chat process, enabling you to transfer data seamlessly between LoyJoy and SFSC. This module allows you to create, update, and read objects, such as Person, Case, or custom objects, in Salesforce. Typical Use Cases​ Data Management: Use this module to create or update objects like Cases or Contacts in Salesforce based on data collected during the chat. Customer Support: Implement a Web-to-Case system where customer requests are automatically turned into cases in SFSC. How to Use the Module​ Modes​ SObject (write): Write data to Salesforce objects (e.g., Case, Person). You just need the name of the object and the name of the field you want to write to configure the transfer. Option to update only existing records or create new ones. Requires authorization using Client ID, Secret, and Salesforce domain name. Supports mappings to align chat variables with Salesforce fields. Example Mapping​ SObject (read): Retrieve data from Salesforce objects. Requires authorization and supports mappings. API Request: Perform custom API requests to Salesforce. Requires authorization and mappings. Chat: Initiate a Salesforce Service Cloud chat session. Requires Deployment ID, Organization ID, Button ID, and Salesforce deployment domain. Web-to-Case​ Support requests from customers can also be recorded and auto\",\"imgs\":[\"sF1-aaa6274d97bdd3c0617cac28cfee043e.png|grafik\",\"sfsc_wtc1-30b72036c7731b28967ceb159c561206.png|sfsc_wtc1\",\"sF2-8fa4176a23d09ba6549a8364c04faf83.png|grafik\",\"sF3-83c25a73904ed20343fc74b774f89e19.png|grafik\",\"sF6-d333018073ccb1e3cf369712822d208b.png|grafik\",\"sF8-1b1a90f89cc74d5fec0c70a68286a884.png|grafik\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/scanner/\",\"len\":1613,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesScanner ModuleOn this pageScanner Module Introduction​ The Scanner module enables your customers to scan QR codes or barcodes using their device's camera or manually enter the code if they prefer. This ensures that all users can interact with your products, regardless of their device capabilities or personal preference. Typical Use Cases​ This module is useful for providing additional product information, such as ingredients, origin details, or installation videos. How to Use the Module​ Guiding the Customer​ Tell your customer where to find the code and that they can either scan it using their device's camera or manually enter it into the provided field. Including a picture to illustrate this can be helpful. Customizing Responses​ Categories: Use categories to differentiate responses based on the scanned or entered code. Each unique response requires a separate category. Response Types: For each category, set up one of the following response types: Text response with an animation Video response Automatic or decision jump to another module Optional Settings​ You can enable an option to allow customers to skip the scanning step if they prefer. Useful tips​ The following variable is created in this module: ${scanner_code}. This variable can be used to reference the scanned or entered code in subsequent steps or responses. Process-Specific Variables​ This module generates variables that are accessible throughout the current process. They are only valid for this speci\",\"imgs\":[\"scanner-1aca914310eec9f4b53b4396e81a0894.png|scanner\",\"w8XF0mLXJMr6AAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==|scanner_skip\"],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0},{\"u\":\"/bpmn/subprocesses/scanner/scanner/\",\"len\":1963,\"t\":\"BPMN ModulesScanner ModuleHow to Set up a Barcode Scanner ProcessOn this pageHow to Set up a Barcode Scanner Process What This Solution Will Do for You​ In this article we explain how to set up a process where users can scan a product's barcode and get information on it. What You Need for This Solution to Work​ You will need two things to implement this article: A product feed microservice and its URL & endpoints Data of your specific products in the feed (prefix, shop-directory, url) Set up the Process​ You can also copy a finished process from a toolbox. Then you only have to change the specific parameters in webservice process bricks (see below). Add a Snapshot Process Module​ This snapshot process module will present the user with the option to scan a barcode. Add one category and enter * as the recognized barcode. This will recognize all barcodes as belonging to this category. Add a Webservice Process Module​ In this webservice we will send the recognized barcode to our product feed microservice. It will then create a message with information about the product for us. It will also create some process variables, that we will use later on. You will need to enter the URL of the microservice as well as the parameters the microservice requires. These parameters are usually: NamePurposeauthenticationVerifying that we are allowed to call the microserviceprefixPrefix of your specific products (e.g. country code)shopName of the shop directory on your URLurlURL of your website, li\",\"imgs\":[],\"links\":[],\"hits\":[],\"nh\":0}]"